# Trivy findings accepted for now in images this repo owns (third-party images pinned by digest in Terraform). The
# nightly Image Scan (running images) accepts a finding only with a row in the root exception register
# docs/security/vuln-exceptions.toml (repo AA-CIS-Infra, source trivy); this file mirrors those rows with the same
# expiry so the monthly triage can cross-check them (root SEC-03). The nightly gate never reads this file:
# tools/security/image_scan.py passes an empty --ignorefile to every Trivy call, since an entry here has no repo scope
# and would hide the CVE in every running image, not only the ones this repo owns. Format:
#
#   # <reason: why it is safe for now, and what removes it>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# No entry today. AA-1185 (S296): the WordPress test sidecar no longer runs (the Booking admin task has one container
# since the S295 sweep), so its libzstd1 exception and the matching root register row were removed.
